==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Major Space Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Space Marine Cat''' when obtained from [[Revenge of R-Cyclone (Deadly)|Revenge of R-Cyclone]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
At first sight, Space Cat seems like an underwhelming Cat; it has very low health, low attack and a very low chance for a Critical Hit (4%). However, this units' strengths are that it has long range, a relatively fast recharge time and a low cost, meaning you can stack it easily. It's useful when behind meatshields in very large numbers, so it can destroy most [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies quite quickly by outnumbering them.

With its range, it's very helpful in defeating Metal enemies with strong backline attackers where short-ranged Critical Hitters are easily killed, such as in [[Mysterious Order]] and [[Old Guys in the City (Monthly Event)|Old Guys in the City]] stages. It can also save a slot in [[N77 Nebula (Cats of the Cosmos)|N77 Nebula]], where it can take advantage of both its critting and barrier breaking abilities.

==='''True Form'''===
Space Marine Cat is a massive improvement over the previous forms, as its usefulness against Metals doubles alongside its Critical chance. In addition, it becomes a more reliable Barrier Breaker and tends to survive longer with better health, further improving its usefulness. However, at this point in the game it is outclassed by [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]], but is still a great secondary Critter and Barrier Breaker, even more so in {{4c}} stages.

Space Marine Cat also gains access to a new combo, [[Warriors of Justice (Combo)|Warriors of Justice]]. While it isn't the best combo out there, it makes [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast]] much more effective, so if you can use it, maybe try bringing it to an especially hard [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] stage.

