==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.3 Update#Version 2.3.1 Update|Version 2.3.1]] increased Space Cat's [[Critical Hit]] chance from 1% to 3%.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Major Space Cat was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Triggermen (Removed Combo)|Triggermen]].
*[[Version 5.6 Update|Version 5.6]] increased Space Cat's Critical Hit chance further from 3% to 4%, but reduced the Evolved Form's stats to 3,060 health and 1,207 attack, matching the Normal Form. The stat nerfs were reverted in [[Version 6.5 Update|Version 6.5]].
*Space Cat was among the units that were given [[Barrier Breaker]] in Version 6.5.
**Of these Cats, Space Cat is the only one to have it in all forms.
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Space Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Space Cat
Coming out of his shuttle to attack.
Low health, but can break Barriers!
Might perform critical attacks.</pre>
<pre>Major Space Cat
Recently promoted from Lieutenant.
Low health, but can break Barriers!
Might perform critical attacks.</pre>
<pre>Space Marine Cat
The ultimate in zero-gravity combat tech,
deployed to preserve the glory of the Cat Empire!
Breaks Barriers, might perform critical attacks.</pre>
*The stats of this Cat are almost exactly the same as [[Archer Cat (Rare Cat)|Archer Cat]], except that it can do a [[Critical Hit|Critical Attack]] instead of Massive Damage to [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies.
*The Evolved Form is reference a [[wikia:gundam:Char Aznable|Char Aznable]] in his pilot suit, as he holds lieutenant rank on the original MS Gundam anime. The red color and horn on the helmet are his distinctive characteristics.
*The True Form might be a reference to [[wikia:halo:John-117|Master Chief]] from the Halo franchise or Space Marines from the Warhammer 40,000 franchise.

